# Build-context exclusions for backend/Dockerfile*, whose `COPY . /app/`
# would otherwise bake these runtime directories into the image.
#
# media/ and staticfiles/ are named-volume mount points, not build input:
# docker-compose.yml mounts `media_volume` at /app/media on backend, celery
# and firmware_builder, and Docker seeds a freshly created named volume from
# the image content at the mount point. With media/ in the image, `compose
# up` creates those containers in parallel and each copies the same tree into
# the same empty volume, so the loser of the race fails to start with
#   failed to mkdir .../openmakersuite_media_volume/_data/inventory: file exists
# Keeping the mount points empty in the image means there is nothing to seed.
media
staticfiles
